  "practice": [
    "Say ড three times with the tongue curled slightly backward: ḍô, ḍô, ḍô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: ড (ḍô), ডা (ḍa), ডি (ḍi), ডী (ḍi, uncommon), ডু (ḍu), ডূ (ḍu, rare), ডে (ḍe), ডৈ (ḍoi, rare), ডো (ḍo), and ডৌ (ḍou, rare).",
    "Read the combinations aloud: ড + া = ডা as in ডাক, ড + ি = ডি as in ডিম, ড + ু = ডু as in ডুব, ড + ে = ডে as in ডেটা, and ড + ো = ডো as in ডোজ.",
    "Compare ড (ḍ) with ঢ (ḍh, extra air): ডাল / ঢাল, ডাক / ঢাকা, ডিম / ঢেউ, and ডান / ঢোকা.",
    "Use ডাক, ডাকা, ডাক্তার, ডাল, ডিম, ডান, ডানা, ডাব, and ডুব as quick reading anchors.",
    "Break down ডাক্তারকে ডাকো: ডাক্তার means doctor, কে is the object marker, and ডাকো means call."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ড is a common Bangla consonant named ḍô. Its sound resembles d, but the tongue curls slightly backward.",
    "ড and ঢ are closely related: ড has a ḍ sound, while ঢ has an aspirated ḍh sound with a stronger burst of air.",
    "Compare ডাল (ḍal, lentils), ডাক (ḍak, call), ডিম (ḍim, egg), and ডান (ḍan, right) with ঢাল (ḍhal, slope/shield), ঢাকা (ḍhaka, Dhaka), ঢেউ (ḍheu, wave), and ঢোকা (ḍhoka, enter).",
    "Best words to memorize include ডাক্তার, ডাকা, ডাক, ডাল, ডিম, ডান, ডানা, ডাব, ডুবা, ডুবে, ডুবুরি, ডলার, ডজন, ডিগ্রি, ড্রাইভার, ড্রাইভ, ডেটা, and ডেস্ক."
